ed for a YouTube citation whose payload carries a supplied transcript snippet (single-line snippet, the existing mockCitation shape in CitationModal.test.tsx)","id":"AC-1","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal","then":"inside the dialog (role=\"dialog\", aria-label \"Video citation\"), a section headed 'Transcript Excerpt' appears below the video player block, and its text block contains the citation's supplied snippet text verbatim; the YouTube player iframe (title \"YouTube video player\") is still rendered alongside it","when":"the modal renders"},{"given":"the citation modal is rendered for a YouTube citation whose snippet contains literal newline characters between caption lines","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal","then":"the snippet's exact supplied text appears in the 'Transcript Excerpt' section with every line intact and no truncation, trimming or reformatting (matched with a whitespace-preserving query, e.g. exact textContent equality or a no-op normalizer), and the element carrying it has a computed white-space of pre-wrap (set as an inline style, so the literal line breaks render as separate lines rather than one collapsed paragraph)","when":"the modal renders"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Kept modal behaviour is unchanged (issue hard constraint): embed URL with start and autoplay params, video title, timestamp range, 'Open on YouTube' external link with t param, Escape-key close, close-button close, backdrop-click close, and body-scroll lock while mounted. These are covered by the existing untouched unit tests in CitationModal.test.tsx and must still pass.","Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea.handleCitationClick opens lesson_url directly); citation chips and tooltips in Message.tsx are unchanged.","The snippet is displayed from the Citation payload as supplied — the change is presentation-only; no backend, ingest, API or schema change, and no client-side truncation or reformatting of snippet content.","The pre-existing unit test 'does not render a transcript snippet section' (app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx:35-41) pins the old behaviour AC-1 and AC-2 replace and must be rewritten inside the same acceptance-test file during the RED stage; it cannot survive unchanged.","Apart from that rewritten test and the two new AC checkpoints, the remaining tests in CitationModal.test.tsx (kept-behaviour tests and formatTimestamp tests) stay byte-identical, and __tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx and Message.test.tsx need no change.","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit are untouched; all existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory (issue hard constraint)."],"issue":{"number":181,"title":"Citation inspection [transcript]"},"out_of_scope":["Keyboard focus management into/out of the modal on open/close — this is programme part 2 of citation-inspection (a separate later step with no AC in this issue); existing Escape behaviour is preserved, not extended.","The Dynamous citation path (never routed to the modal) and Message.tsx chips/tooltips.","Any backend, ingest, API or schema change to snippet sourcing, length or content.","New content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory-authority changes or external dependencies (issue out-of-scope).","Modal width/layout redesign beyond adding the snippet section to the existing scrollable content column.","Modifying frozen acceptance tests from prior builds, protected files, or any proof/permission rule."],"risks":["Whitespace-matching trap (this issue's own failed build 34998691864): an exact getByText on multiline text under Testing Library's default whitespace normalizer can never match literal newlines. The AC-2 checkpoint must use a whitespace-preserving normalizer or exact textContent equality and must keep the expected text verbatim rather than reflowing it.","Mis-declared expected_failure burns the single RED hand-back (D-069); the test author has no shell, so declare short literal fragments of Testing Library's stable error (e.g. 'Unable to find an element with the text'), quote-free and immune to formatting.","A Tailwind-class-only pre-wrap implementation is unobservable in jsdom (class rules have no stylesheet); the snippet element must carry the pre-wrap behaviour as an inline style so getComputedStyle reflects it and AC-2's display assertion is strong.","Stale negative test: if the contradicting unit test survives the RED commit, GREEN fails late (after the implement commit) with no cheap recovery.","Attempt budget: max_attempts is 2 and this is the programme's second build of issue #181, so a second validation failure escalates to a human; keep the change minimal (one product file plus one test file, no dependency or docs churn)."],"summary":"Render the citation's supplied transcript snippet inside the citation modal below the video player, under a 'Transcript Excerpt' heading, verbatim with an inline white-space: pre-wrap style so multiline snippets keep their line breaks; presentation-only change to CitationModal.tsx plus a rewrite of the contradicting unit test.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"9c913dea3437b5fd99eb88c16d43b0a75296f8196af5b8c8a215e7585b2abdb0","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"66c814a0925786e21efa18b466bcbadb4414ada7c9fb2c4afd387e57e660f3f0","contract_sha256":"9c913dea3437b5fd99eb88c16d43b0a75296f8196af5b8c8a215e7585b2abdb0","data_flows":["Citation.snippet (verbatim, may contain literal newlines) -> CitationModal -> 'Transcript Excerpt' section text block rendered with inline white-space: pre-wrap","ChatArea.selectedCitation (YouTube citations only) -> ChatArea.handleCitationClick -> CitationModal rendered dialog (header, YouTube iframe, Transcript Excerpt section, footer link)"],"invariants":["Kept modal behaviour unchanged: embed URL with start and autoplay params, video title, timestamp range, 'Open on YouTube' external link with t param, Escape-key close, close-button close, backdrop-click close, and body-scroll lock while mounted — all existing untouched unit tests in CitationModal.test.tsx must still pass.","Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea.handleCitationClick opens lesson_url directly); citation chips and tooltips in Message.tsx are unchanged.","The snippet is displayed from the Citation payload as supplied — presentation-only; no backend, ingest, API or schema change, and no client-side truncation or reformatting of snippet content.","The pre-existing unit test 'does not render a transcript snippet section' (CitationModal.test.tsx:35-41) is rewritten inside the same acceptance-test file during the RED stage and cannot survive unchanged.","Apart from that rewritten test and the two new AC checkpoints, the remaining tests in CitationModal.test.tsx (kept-behaviour tests and formatTimestamp tests) stay byte-identical; __tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx and Message.test.tsx need no change.","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit are untouched; all existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory."],"modules":["CitationModal"],"planned_files":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx"],"public_interfaces":["CitationModal({ citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element (role=\"dialog\", aria-label \"Video citation\")"],"seams":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal"],"version":"1.0"},"sha256":"ffe2b7b8721d3ac95afc6e06dc077747784253f9ff4df8b75c08608983644f45","source":"design.json"},"frontier":{"content":{"accepted":true,"blockers":[],"issue":181,"ready":true,"ticket_sha256":"836b